#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""webby - a dependency-free terminal web browser (Python 3 standard library only).

Usage:  webby [options] [url | file | search words]

Features
  * HTML rendering with wrapped text, headings, lists, tables, quotes, code,
    links, forms (text fields, checkboxes, radios, selects, buttons), cookies,
    redirects, gzip, charset detection, meta-refresh, file:// and data: URLs.
  * Mouse support (SGR mode): click links / fields / toolbar buttons, wheel to
    scroll, hover shows the link target.
  * Inline images on terminals that can show them: the kitty graphics protocol
    (kitty, Ghostty, ...) and the iTerm2 inline image protocol (iTerm2,
    WezTerm, mintty, ...).  Kitty needs PNG, so JPEG/GIF/WebP are converted
    with `magick`/`convert`/`sips` when one of them is installed (sips ships
    with macOS).  Elsewhere images are shown as [alt text].

Keys (press ? in the browser for the full list)
  g / Ctrl-L  go to URL (or search)     b / Left   back      f / Right  forward
  j k / arrows / PgUp PgDn / Space      scroll     Tab       next link/field
  Enter       follow focused item       /  n  N    search    r  reload
  i           toggle images             d          save page   q  quit
  t x [ ] 1-9 new / close / switch tabs (middle-click a link: background tab)
  B M H       bookmark page / bookmarks / history      l  list links
  R           reader mode (just the article)       C  toggle CSS
"""

